  READ THE EX-ANTE ROW CAREFULLY. Under this cost model realized PnL is a
  DETERMINISTIC function of gap, prices and spread, so 'take iff gross > cost'
  selects exactly the profitable trades and will show a 100% win rate BY
  CONSTRUCTION. That is not a forecasting result. It is the upper bound on
  what any selection rule can achieve GIVEN PERFECT KNOWLEDGE OF THE SPREAD,
  and the spread here is a period aggregate, not a live quote. The gap between
  this row and reality is exactly the error in forecasting execution cost --
  which is the only unobservable term in the equation, and therefore the only
  place a learned model can contribute anything at all.

  If the gap-top-N rows go negative here while the model row survives,
  the large-gap 'opportunities' were spread artifacts and selection matters.
  If every row goes negative, the strategy does not clear real execution
  costs and THAT is the finding -- consistent with the ~1% exploitation
  rate reported for apparent arbitrage on zero-fee Polymarket.
